# Secrets — never commit these.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Real user data. The seeded demo database is built by a script, not committed.
data/*.db
data/*.db-wal
data/*.db-shm
data/export_*.json

# Python
.venv/
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.tiktoken_cache/

# Node / Vite
node_modules/
frontend/.vite/

# frontend/dist IS committed, deliberately.
#
# Build artefacts in git are normally wrong. Here they remove Node from the grader's
# path entirely: clone, create a venv, pip install, run — and the whole interface is
# there. The assignment scores "the teaching staff can run it" and gives ten minutes,
# and an npm install is the single most likely way to lose that.
#
# The cost is staleness. After changing anything under frontend/src you MUST run
# `npm run build` and commit the result, or the app serves the old interface. /api/health
# reports `frontend_built` so at least its absence is visible.

# Demo-mode eval output.
#
# Regenerable in seconds with `python -m backend.run_evals all`, and worthless as
# evidence — a demo run makes no model call, so it grades nothing about the agents.
# Keeping it out of the repo means the only eval artefacts a reader can find in
# output/ are ones a live run actually produced.
output/demo_runs/

# OS
.DS_Store

# TypeScript build cache. Regenerated on every build; no reason to ship it.
frontend/tsconfig.tsbuildinfo

# The prompt log stays on disk and out of the repo.
#
# AI_prompts.md records Christine's own prompts verbatim — including a personal
# disclosure, her mother's text messages, and candid working language. The repo went
# public on 2026-11-23 so the teaching staff could clone it, and the course
# requirements never asked for a prompt log: it is a workspace convention from
# AGENTS.md, not a final-project deliverable. It was removed from all 91 commits of
# history at the same time, not just untracked going forward, because making a repo
# public publishes every commit.
#
# The file itself still lives beside this one. Keep writing it.
AI_prompts.md
.prompt-log-backup/

# A 620 KB SQLite file the _seed_on_boot test left in the repo root on 2026-11-20 and
# that got swept into a commit on that date. Synthetic demo data only, no secrets — clutter
# rather than a leak, but not something a grader should clone.
tmp*/

# Screen recordings. The demo video is a Canvas upload, not a repo file — and a 130 MB
# .mov landing in the project folder is one `git add -A` away from being committed into
# a submission whose instructions say any extra file will be penalized.
*.mov
*.mp4
*.m4v
